{"user": "so next time get corners?", "user_ts": "2026-08-26T14:47:50.463518+00:00", "assistant": "Yes \u2014 **corners are huge**, because once you get a corner it **can never be flipped**.\n\nBut not just \u201cgrab corners\u201d \u2014 the bigger rule is:\n\n- **Take a corner when available.**\n- **Avoid playing next to an empty corner** unless you\u2019ve calculated it\u2019s safe.\n  - \u201cX-squares\u201d: **b2, g2, b7, g7**\n  - \u201cC-squares\u201d: **a2, b1, g1, h2, a7, b8, g8, h7**\n- In the endgame, look for moves that **leave White with few moves** or force White to give you a corner.\n- Don\u2019t just flip the most discs immediately.\n\nSo: **corners first, but mobility and not handing over corners matter just as much.**", "assistant_started_ts": "2026-08-26T14:47:52.713413+00:00", "assistant_ts": "2026-08-26T14:47:55.159534+00:00", "annotation_user": {"final": ["Think Aloud", "Common Ground Question", "Solution Request"], "consensus": [], "votes": {"Solution Request": 1, "Common Ground Question": 1, "Think Aloud": 1}, "confidence": {"Solution Request": 0.3333333333333333, "Common Ground Question": 0.3333333333333333, "Think Aloud": 0.3333333333333333}, "per_model": {"gpt": ["Solution Request"], "sonnet": ["Common Ground Question"], "llama": ["Think Aloud"]}, "n_valid": 3, "min_votes": 2, "no_majority": true, "needs_review": true, "arbiter_used": false}, "annotation_assistant_fine": {"final": ["General Principle"], "consensus": ["General Principle"], "votes": {"General Principle": 3, "Positive Feedback": 1}, "confidence": {"General Principle": 1.0, "Positive Feedback": 0.3333333333333333}, "per_model": {"gpt": ["General Principle"], "sonnet": ["General Principle", "Positive Feedback"], "llama": ["General Principle"]}, "n_valid": 3, "min_votes": 2, "no_majority": false, "needs_review": false, "arbiter_used": false, "coarse": ["Direct Instruction"]}}
